{
	title: 'A restart reconnects clients within about a second',
	spec: 'After a restart the new host serves the Unix socket and the web within about a second, however many tabs are open, and no session size delays it. Work over every open tab (restart notes, project plugins, turn recovery, lost background jobs) runs after the web listens, a tab at a time, and reads only history tails: pages.findLast reads backwards. Settings recovery after a rebase runs once per rebase (meta.settledRebase). Web clients retry a lost connection at most 1 s apart (wsLink.maxDelayMs), and every 0.25 s for 30 s after a restart. The systemd unit restarts after 100 ms.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'Bug fix invariant: nothing that grows with open-tab count runs between taking the host lock and web.start. Before: becomeHost awaited projectContext.refresh and restartNote.announce, which opened all 174 tabs (sessionSettings.recover parsed every full history, uncached because the session was not yet open), so the web listened 7.5-8.7 s after start; web pages then backed off up to 15 s (10 s cap with jitter) and missed it. Measured on the server with a copy of the 175 open sessions: web on after 10.5 s before, 1.2 s after.',
		'Remaining: a big rebased session (07-lou, 27 MB) still blocks up to ~1.2 s while restartNote and prompt-files catchUp open it (pages.rebased replay, full parse); slicing within one session belongs to task 7j.',
		'Supersedes the Remaining note: idle sessions no longer cost startup time. restartNote and prompt-cache interactive read history tails via pages.findLast; recover skips sessions whose meta.settledRebase matches marks. Measured on the server with the 175-session copy: web on 169-556 ms, worst web response during startup work 243 ms. findLast matched readSync on all 175 sessions (one-off check).'
	],
	needs: ['2e', 'tr']
}
